10. MEMORY ALLOCATION: PROCEDURAL VS OOP

Procedural Programming:
- Memory mainly stores variables and functions.
- Memory usage is relatively low.
- Uses Stack Memory.

OOP:
- Objects are created in Heap Memory.
- Each object stores attributes and method references.
- Objects consume more memory because every object stores its own state.

Procedural vs OOP:
Procedural - Less memory, variables + functions
OOP - More memory, objects + attributes